Z||000000||TRL46202||03-09-2000||10:09 AM||||I just spoke to Tim and he said that he is still going to go through with the Borla system but the people that promised to send a check (30+)still haven't done so, only 2 and I will send mine today so 3. Disregard to previous post on this topic!! and send your money in, the people that said they would know who I'm talking about.....||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||03-09-2000||11:13 AM||||Sorry to say this but at this rate we may have the 20 needed somewhere in 2001. I'm not willing to wait that long. Tim called everybody more than two weeks ago. 31 long distance calls is a lot of commitment from him and I appreciate that effort. Looks like very few people here seems interested (having resource$) in the system with the feedback to these threads. That to me is an indicator. Really hope it get through soon for the rest.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierosound||03-09-2000||03:25 PM||||There may be others waiting for the announcement that "only 3 are left" before making the commitment to purchase. They may get the attitude "it ain't gonna go" and hold back. That's what's causing the problem in the first place, the "fence sitters". You know who you are...<P>Tim ONLY needs 17 more people to get this thing built... <P>I know alot of the guys think $420 is too expensive for a Borla stainless steel exhaust system. Check out the price of this stainless steel exhaust system from Fiero Heaven. <A HREF="http://www.fieroheaven.com/Exhaust.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroheaven.com/Exhaust.htm</A>  <P>RS Motorsports also has a stainless steel exhaust system for US$680. <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/</A>  <P>Of course, there's always the Ocelot exhaust from The Fiero Store and GM's stock exhaust system to choose from as well.  A couple of people mentioned the Ocelot system was not all it's cracked up to be.  <A HREF="http://www.secureleadercom.com/fierostore/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secureleadercom.com/fierostore/</A> <P>But at present, the Borla seems to be the best priced of the stainless steel performance exhaust systems. If you check around, Borlas for most other cars START at $400 and go over $1000!!! Check Borla's website!!! <A HREF="http://www.borla.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.borla.com/</A>  <P><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 03-09-2000).]||||reg||10
