Z||000007||mrfiero||03-21-2000||03:38 AM||||Tim at Fiero Parts & Appraisals has an exclusive agreement with Borla to produce a cat back exhaust system for the Pontiac Fiero.  Last year he purchased an entire run of these just to get them done (at an incredibe personal expense).  That run has been sold out and he decided to do another run, however, this time he did not want to foot the bill upfront by himself (I don't blame him).  <P>He  currently needs about 10 more people to step up and send in the money to get this next run produced.  If anyone really wants one give Tim a call at (207) 934-0103.<P>The first run did have Borlas "intercooled" tips on then and the system was around $500.  He had several people state that they wished it did not come with tips as they would be putting their stock GT tips on it anyways. They felt they were wasting money on tips they weren't going to use.  That said, he decided to price this next run without tips.  The price difference, in my opinion, is minimal and I persoanlly would prefer to have the tips on them, but I think it's too late at this point (not 100% sure though, maybe Tim can still get them with tips?).<P>I bought one of the original systems and I can say it is a work of art.  VERY well built and well worth the money.  Unfortunately I resold it as I got into a small financial crisis a few months ago.  Needless to say I'm buying one from this next run!||||reg||1
Z||000008||phillip||03-21-2000||08:54 AM||||i just got a stock(except for tips) g-t exhaust for my 2.5.i got it to put on two big tips i had and also in hope of a bigger engine swap in the future so i can't turn around and get another system.also could'nt convince any shop in the city that there were other options beyond stock. but i'd still like to know the appeal of the borla system. durability because of stainless steel or performance? would it be able to work behind a larger engine better than a stock system?||||reg||1
